cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Registered Backtests: a pre-registered replication of 12 published trading strategies"
message: "If you reference this study, please cite it and note the version, since ERRATA.md records that one headline conclusion changed after review."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Adil
    given-names: Mayher
    affiliation: Connecticut College
repository-code: "https://github.com/mayherprog/registered-backtests"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered replication study of twelve published trading strategies
  against SPY buy-and-hold, using a build window of 2015-2022 split into four
  two-year folds and a held-out validation window of 2023-2026. Rules, costs,
  data approximations and the pass criterion were registered before any
  simulation was run. Two strategies clear the original registered gate; neither
  survives a second gate, registered before computation, that matches the
  benchmark to each strategy's own capital exposure. A code review documented in
  ERRATA.md found seven defects, three material, including one in the Sortino
  denominator that had suppressed the two passes and one incorrect claim about
  the held-out data.
keywords:
  - pre-registration
  - backtesting
  - replication
  - quantitative finance
  - reproducibility
  - null results
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
